# Two independent pendulums off the base -- loop-free, cheap -- carrying a
# TSDA from a fixed base point to a point on body 0's rod, and an RSDA on
# body 1's joint, both declared 'input'. Exercises every force-element code
# path (POI kinematics, TSDA path-walk with a and c and act, RSDA with k, c
# and act) without the added complexity of a kinematic loop; see
# slidercrank.mech for a model combining elements with a loop.

gravity 0 0 -9.81

body                     # 0: pendulum swinging about y, TSDA attaches here
parent -1
joint revolute y
tree 0 0 0
mass 1
cg 0 0 -0.5
inertia 0.08 0.08 0.01 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 1: pendulum swinging about x, RSDA acts on this joint
parent -1
joint revolute x
tree 1 0 0
mass 0.7
cg 0 0 -0.4
inertia 0.05 0.05 0.008 0 0 0

poi topAnchor -1 0 0 0.5    # fixed point above body 0's pivot
poi bob 0 0 0 -1             # bottom of body 0's rod

tsda spring
from topAnchor
to bob
k 40
c 2
l0 1.0
input

rsda damper
joint 1
k 5
c 0.5
q0 0
input
